{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1005160-non-canon-exploration","id":1005160,"title":"Non-canon exploration???","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-18T17:12:38-08:00","id":1005160,"title":"Non-canon exploration???","content":"I just got an email from DriveThruRPG that says Shattered Dreams is &quot;a non-canon exploration of a wild and crazy vision of the World of Darkness.&quot; I don't understand. I'm not usually a girl who swears, but why the hell am I going to pay fifteen dollars for something that isn't even canon history? And I was so looking forward to this book...can someone please explain this to me? Thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T17:21:36-08:00","id":1005161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JulianMoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1005160-non-canon-exploration#post1005160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just got an email from DriveThruRPG that says Shattered Dreams is &quot;a non-canon exploration of a wild and crazy vision of the World of Darkness.&quot; I don't understand. I'm not usually a girl who swears, but why the hell am I going to pay fifteen dollars for something that isn't even canon history? And I was so looking forward to this book...can someone please explain this to me? Thanks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shattered Dreams involves time travel and alternate causalities; it was never meant to be a history book. From what I can tell, it is more like a presentation of different settings, all of which are potentially subject to deviation from canon. You need empty space for the players to accomplish their goals, and in order to have tension, the outcome of their actions should not be predetermined.<br /> <br /> If the book only included canon events and forced people to enact them, it would suck as a setting. Would you want to play in an Impergium or Dragon Kings timeline where your actions are fixed and nothing you do will alter the already established canon? I wouldn't. Nobody likes a sandbox someone has already shit in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 11-18-2016, 08:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T17:28:09-08:00","id":1005166,"title":"","content":"Ok, you've got a point there. Have you read the book yet? Is there at least a default timeline your characters can modify by their actions? I'm sorry, I'm a historian as much as a gamer, and a sense of tragedy is very important to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T17:37:04-08:00","id":1005167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JulianMoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1005160-non-canon-exploration?p=1005166#post1005166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, you've got a point there. Have you read the book yet? Is there at least a default timeline your characters can modify by their actions? I'm sorry, I'm a historian as much as a gamer, and a sense of tragedy is very important to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>No need to apologize, I just read an early kickstarter beta. Unfortunately I do not have the new copy in hand. I strongly suspect one of my players is getting me it for Christmas (yey!).<br /> <br /> I think the time travel idea is presented so that you can play characters in the present day with all of the setting defaults/canon, and then go back and fix... something. I think it was Nightmaster the crazy Shadow Lord who is up to time-warping shenanigans in the Abyss and you have to stop him from meddling in the war of rage? I am pretty sure I read something along those lines, but who knows, that might have changed in the final iteration of the book.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T23:11:42-08:00","id":1005622,"title":"","content":"Frankly, it's a weird label that feels slapped on as an afterthought, because nothing in the book suggests that the rough ideas presented are anything but 'canon' insofar as any history of the world is canon. In fact, let me quote the one time the book itself addresses the matter - other than an editorial note inserted by New White Wolf's Karim Muamar, that is.<br /> <br /> Prehistory as depicted in this book diverges somewhat from its presentation in other W20 books. This is a deliberate choice \u2014 those books reveal what current shapeshifters believe happened in prehistory, which is quite different from what actually happened. Even the powerful Mnesis of the Mokol\u00e9 isn\u2019t perfect, and is shaped through the understandings of those doing the remembering. This chapter and the next also allow for a War of Rage that starts any time between 70,000 BCE and 2,000 BCE, allowing the Storyteller and players to pick the point in history that most appeals to them. Some groups may not want to have the War of Rage as a full-on running battle, instead using this chapter as a view of how the world decayed naturally over time.<br /> <br /> Some players may wonder what the \u201ccanon\u201d answer is, which choice is most true. That question can\u2019t be answered. Enough about the prehistory of the World of Darkness is already bizarre and contradictory that picking one interpretation of the true history doesn\u2019t work. The truth is, and will always be, what the Storyteller decides.&quot;<br /> <br /> Personally, I'm using what Shattered Dreams gives us as reasonably accurate history for the purpose of my timeline and the Project despite the disclaimer, because in that passage we simultaneously have two outlooks. One, we can't say what is canon and isn't - that decision belongs to the individual storyteller (only now it doesn't, because nWW has that privilege). Two, this is more accurate than what the other books say.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T02:52:45-08:00","id":1005646,"title":"","content":"Yep. That sidebar surprised us all. Certainly me.<br /> Obviously White Wolf has their own ideas and plans, and I imagine (pure supposition here) that since this was the first OPP book to go to WW for approval, there must have been quite some discussion about what WW should do with a book far removed from their expectations or what-have-you. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Anyway, while I was disappointed to see the side-bar put in and the non-canonicity established after so much hard work getting the material to mesh with as much previous information as possible, I'm seriously stoked to see it in print at last and am happy that WW agreed to simply insert a note, rather than cancel it completely.<br /> <br /> I hope people enjoy it and use it in their games regardless. And if anyone makes some part canon at their own table, that's wonderful. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'd love to work more on it. So many ideas there wasn't space for, nor time to develop.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T03:18:20-08:00","id":1005648,"title":"","content":"I'd more than welcome any scraps you have from the cutting room floor, Nik. 'Apocrypha' and explanatory notes are huge boons for the Project. And since the canon notice wasn't something you were all expecting to be there, that just further affirms my decision to treat Shattered Dreams as the (loosely, at least) accurate version of the past for my purposes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T12:28:39-08:00","id":1005803,"title":"","content":"Well, I wouldn't know where to begin. But if you have questions I can maybe give my non-canonical answers. Stick to The War of Rage and War of Tears for accuracy, since I worked on those specifically.<br /> <br /> One thing I wish I could have fit in was an description of humanities progress over time. A way to 'set the scene' for each era, which would have (hopefully) given players a sense of the period, and why Homid Changing Breeds were such an advantage during times when the majority of shapeshifters were &lt;Animal&gt; breeds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T13:30:24-08:00","id":1005835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nikink</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1005160-non-canon-exploration?p=1005803#post1005803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I wouldn't know where to begin. But if you have questions I can maybe give my non-canonical answers. Stick to The War of Rage and War of Tears for accuracy, since I worked on those specifically.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, I had to stop reading the War of Tears section at parts, because the way the Aborginals were treated was really really sad. A good thing, because the variatety of treatments each tribe had and the use of alcohol and drugs is a far more tragic fall than being killed outright. Nevermind the lost generations. Good job!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T14:45:26-08:00","id":1005864,"title":"","content":"Wow, thanks. I'm glad it had an effect. It was heartbreaking to write about and I did my best to be conscious of and respectful of the tragedy and the real people involved.<br /> <br /> Sometimes it's all too easy to say 'The Wyrm made this happen'. But take away the WoD-isms, and this shit really happened to real people because of real people. Truly awful. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T20:28:59-08:00","id":1005957,"title":"","content":"Was there any plan to explore the growing evidence of sophisticated pre-contact agriculture down here in Shattered Dreams? If the case put forth by Pascoe has any accuracy at all, it was one hell of a system with a different modality to settled agriculture in other parts of the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T23:55:21-08:00","id":1006027,"title":"","content":"Where is 'down here'? I assume you mean Australia?<br /> <br /> But, no plans as such. Wasn't on-topic enough to cover the rise of Agriculture in depth - let alone in multiple places around the world. I did what I could to get the proto-Bunyip in place with the first people to arrive in Australia, and to explain why and how they lost their wolf kin, and gave a rough (hopefully plausible) start to what would become a terrible enmity with the Ananasi. Of course, as more evidence for the date of human arrival is uncovered, my placement of between 70kya and 50kya will either be supported or blown away as naive or dumb.<br /> <br /> I squeezed in references to ancient contact with Indonesian islanders along with the arrival of the dingo in the Bunyip history, but couldn't quite get in a mention of aboriginal settlements iirc. (Been a while <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> I had a mental outline of the rise of cities and the vampires within, around the middle-east, India, and the Wan Xian et al in eastern Asia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T23:56:28-08:00","id":1006029,"title":"","content":"Perhaps the eventual Bunyip tribe-book will cover that aspect of history. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T23:57:15-08:00","id":1006030,"title":"","content":"Yes, I'm one of those damnable Aussies so 'down here' is Australia.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> I rather hope it will. It would make an incredible counterpoint to the rest of the setting's 'agriculture badddd' stance (I know I'm generalizing and simplifying there) to have a nation-wide system of agriculture that didn't create societal evils and actually perpetuated a way of life in fine symbiosis with the landscape and the spiritual world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T10:23:34-08:00","id":1006263,"title":"","content":"Thank you all for responding. I'm definitely going to pick up Shattered Dreams and use my discretion as to what is and isn't &quot;canon&quot; in my chronicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T12:14:34-08:00","id":1006323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1005160-non-canon-exploration?p=1006030#post1006030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, I'm one of those damnable Aussies so 'down here' is Australia.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> I rather hope it will. It would make an incredible counterpoint to the rest of the setting's 'agriculture badddd' stance (I know I'm generalizing and simplifying there) to have a nation-wide system of agriculture that didn't create societal evils and actually perpetuated a way of life in fine symbiosis with the landscape and the spiritual world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting thought. Certainly the Aussie Shapeshifters existed in reasonable harmony with the Australian Aboriginal tribes - even the Ananasi who objected to their Sylies being burned down occasionally.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, it could, perhaps, be argued that Aboriginal agriculture was no better or worse than that of other human cultures at the time, just with different changing breed politics around it. At some point most of the megafauna was killed - presumably by human hunting, perhaps also by humans altering the countryside by burning off - by mistake or purpose.<br /> <br /> I'd be very wary of falling into racist stereotypes like 'the noble savage' or 'wise primitives', basically. Incidentally, avoiding that crap is why I thought up a specific reason for the Bunyip to be considered and called 'peaceful' by the other Garou during the War of Tears, while trying to show they were not - they were still Gaia's Warriors, after all.<br /> <br /> But I guess we'll see what whoever works on the Bunyip book says. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T17:37:35-08:00","id":1006477,"title":"","content":"I'm very cautious of it as well, though acknowledging the traditional custodian's skill at agriculture and their strong traditional spiritualities should be safe. The symbiotic relationship mention is more to do with the specifics of the agricultural style practiced than it is with anything inherent to the people or the place. It was a largely nomadic system, cycling through multiple sites over a several-year period, and almost more along the lines of ensuring the right things grow than direct cultivation of specific crops (though in some places more direct cultivation than that took place) with the end result of extremely high soil fertility, water retention, and increased biodiversity in contrast to the settled intensivist model's decreasing soil fertility and biodiversity. The one model benefits the ecosystem around it while the other is largely detrimental except where steps are taken to avoid it. Again, this all assumes the growing body of evidence and the hypothesis advanced by Pascoe et al is right.<br /> <br /> The major difference as I see it for the oWoD is that one model becomes an indirect consequence of the impergium, while the other isn't. One developed its specific fixation on getting every last drop of yield out of the land between two factors (regular old human greed and the rebirth of intensivist agriculture as necessary to survive the impergium, due to curtailed land use because angry werewolves keep eating people who wander too far out of town) while the other, largely absent the latter and with the former culturally regulated by customary law and lore, focused on a broader footprint that was not less impactful, but impactful in a less harmful way. The questions are then, 'is this model closer to Gaian teaching?' and 'if not for the Impergium, would it have been practiced elsewhere?' If memory serves, Pascoe also advances a theory from some somewhat scant evidence that there may be the oldest evidence of actual agriculture here, which would certainly be relevant to the question of what role the Impergium played in the development of it elsewhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T20:17:34-08:00","id":1006533,"title":"","content":"That's a fair point. Certainly the Impergium made an impact on human society where it was enacted. Plus the interplay of all the Breeds, which was very different dynamics to the Australian situation.<br /> <br /> Speaking of Impergium, I did have a handy chart of Delirium effects over the course of the War of Rage. Wasn't quite relevant enough to add to the book, since the book doesn't focus on interactions with humanity (or the Impergium) per se. But I did keep it in mind, and how it evolved over the generations, among several geographical regions around the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T20:27:50-08:00","id":1006541,"title":"","content":"If you don't mind, I'd be very interested to see it and incorporate it into my timeline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T21:16:43-08:00","id":1006562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nikink</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1005160-non-canon-exploration?p=1006533#post1006533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Speaking of Impergium, I did have a handy chart of Delirium effects over the course of the War of Rage. Wasn't quite relevant enough to add to the book, since the book doesn't focus on interactions with humanity (or the Impergium) per se. But I did keep it in mind, and how it evolved over the generations, among several geographical regions around the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd also be curious what you had in mind.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T03:42:15-08:00","id":1006645,"title":"","content":"I'll see if I can find it. Don't hold your breath for something amazing though. It's pretty bare bones and rough. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T08:59:29-08:00","id":1006736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nikink</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1005160-non-canon-exploration?p=1005864#post1005864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow, thanks. I'm glad it had an effect. It was heartbreaking to write about and I did my best to be conscious of and respectful of the tragedy and the real people involved.<br /> <br /> Sometimes it's all too easy to say 'The Wyrm made this happen'. But take away the WoD-isms, and this shit really happened to real people because of real people. Truly awful. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry for late reply, but I agree so much. It is easy to write very dark stuff, like the Rage across Australia book did (some accord with the aboriginals wasn't in effect in WoD). But actual cruelty and loss is very hard to deal with, because it is often subtler and with no bigger evil than apathy or ignorance (Fianna in Shattered Dreams, that was awful).<br /> <br /> That is why, when IRL stuff is worse, I use it in WoD.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T15:09:42-08:00","id":1006872,"title":"","content":"Thank you to everyone who has chimed in on this (and other) threads, and everyone who have purchased and read Shattered Dreams. Nik did a *tonne* of research - both real world and WoD - to bring together the snippets of fictional history of the Changing Breeds with factual history spanning thousands of years. He tied together the bits-and-pieces of the War of Tears to make sense of what we knew and the horrors and tragedies of real world history. He didn't shy away from the darkness, and neither did he minimise it, treat it comically, or with disrespect.<br /> <br /> I think he did a great job, and I'm pleased to see others agree. Thanks again, and well done Nik. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T19:11:52-08:00","id":1006960,"title":"","content":"On that note, I do have to express my gratitude for reversing the earlier 'oh it was all because of those darn Black Spiral Dancers that the Bunyip died' cop out fully.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T20:07:46-08:00","id":1006990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1005160-non-canon-exploration?p=1006030#post1006030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, I'm one of those damnable Aussies so 'down here' is Australia.</div> </div> </div> </div>You'll be happy to hear, then, that the two writers of the War of Tears chapter (and a certain War of Dragons co-writer, who <i>totally </i>tagged along on the drafts!) are all damnable Aussies, too. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance OPP. <b>Dark Eras</b>, <b>Shattered Dreams</b>, and counting!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2653-nated","name":"NateD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T20:13:12-08:00","id":1006993,"title":"","content":"I thought I detected a subtle hint of real downunder thunder in that chapter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5307,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","user":"loomer","date":".  Somehow I wrote dedicated, not detected. I blame the heat. 11-23-2016, 01:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T23:47:57-08:00","id":1007064,"title":"","content":"I quite like SD, it's not quite what I was expecting when I first heard the project announced but its pretty good.<br /> <br /> I was wondering if you've gotten any pushback about the Ananasi being behind pretty much every bad thing thats happened since the Pleistocene.<br /> <br /> I would like to thank the folks writing for W20 for their handling of Oz in the WoD...all I need now is to like at least 80% of the Bunyip tribebook and I can forget that RaAus. ever existed. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T04:07:09-08:00","id":1007155,"title":"","content":"We're glad you like it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I've had a search and found some of my notes on the Delirium effect over the centuries. I reiterate the non-canonicity of this idea, and point out it wasn't developed beyond this first thought even though I kept it in mind to inform myself of the state of the world in each setting over time. <div align=\"center\">* * *</div> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Delirium:</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The effects of the Delirium increase over time until they reach modern times. Prior to the Banestorm, Changing Breeds were no scarier in half-man form than animal form. Humans weren\u2019t being singled out and hunted. The humans had no concept of a separation between what was natural and what was supernatural. Post Banestorm as humans were fought over, and the various Kinfolk were hunted by shapeshifters waging war upon each other, the Delirium began. With each generation of humans the effects ever so slowly grew until modern times and modern effects. When the Impergium began the effect grew faster as humans became prey for Garou.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Banestorm:</b> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Delirium does not fully exist, treat all humans as having +7 effective Willpower - except for the Mokole who inflict it normally, including upon the Changing Breeds with the right Gift or Archid Form.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A thousand generations pass.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Migration:</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> For the purposes of calculating the effects of the Delirium treat humans as having +5 to their normal Willpower. Mokole caused Delirium is unaffected.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A thousand generations pass.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Flight and Extinction:</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Calculate the effect of Delirium as if humans have +3 to their normal Willpower. Mokole caused Delirium is unaffected.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A thousand generations pass.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Civilization:</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Calculate the effect of Delirium as if humans have +1 to their normal Willpower. Mokole caused Delirium is unaffected.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Two hundred generations pass.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Deluge:</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Calculate the effect of Delirium as if humans have +1 to their normal Willpower. Mokole caused Delirium is unaffected.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Fifty generations pass.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Poison:</b> Calculate the effect of Delirium as if humans have +1 to their normal Willpower. Mokole caused Delirium is unaffected.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Two hundred generations pass.<br /> <br /> <b>Reconciliation:</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">All backgrounds are now normal</span></span></span> <div align=\"center\">* * *</div> <br /> <br /> So for those interested, there ya go. I can't find where I wrote down my working for this scale, though I vaguely recall doing so. Looks to be every 500 generations of predation decreases the bonus to Willpower by one. Give or take.<br /> <br /> I had similar notes for Caerns, Human Invention, Gifts and Rites available, the Litany's development, Totems, Pure Breed, Ancestors, Fetishes and Talens, geographical ranges for Breeds, Species encompassed by Breeds, the rambling jottings of a timeline, Gauntlet strength, Moon Bridges, Tribe evolution... all sorts of stuff. Some cut for space, some cut for not meshing with other ideas. C'est la vie. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T04:09:44-08:00","id":1007156,"title":"","content":"A-are those other notes NDA or could you share them too? Love this stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><a href=\"http://thecyberrecord.net\" target=\"_blank\">The Cyber Record</a> is on the </span></b><a href=\"http://geomid.network\" target=\"_blank\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Geomid.Network</span></b></a><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Activism is Gaian praxis</span></b></div> <div align=\"right\"> <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><a href=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" ><img itemprop=\"image\" data-align=\"center\" data-linktype=\"1\" data-linkurl=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" data-size=\"full\" border=\"0\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-thumb-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center\" /></a></div><br /> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2810-yakecen-sings","name":"Yakecen-Sings","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2810_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T04:13:34-08:00","id":1007158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nikink</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1005160-non-canon-exploration?p=1007155#post1007155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We're glad you like it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I've had a search and found some of my notes on the Delirium effect over the centuries. I reiterate the non-canonicity of this idea, and point out it wasn't developed beyond this first thought even though I kept it in mind to inform myself of the state of the world in each setting over time. <div align=\"center\">* * *</div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Delirium:</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The effects of the Delirium increase over time until they reach modern times. Prior to the Banestorm, Changing Breeds were no scarier in half-man form than animal form. Humans weren\u2019t being singled out and hunted. The humans had no concept of a separation between what was natural and what was supernatural. Post Banestorm as humans were fought over, and the various Kinfolk were hunted by shapeshifters waging war upon each other, the Delirium began. With each generation of humans the effects ever so slowly grew until modern times and modern effects. When the Impergium began the effect grew faster as humans became prey for Garou.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Banestorm:</b> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Delirium does not fully exist, treat all humans as having +7 effective Willpower - except for the Mokole who inflict it normally, including upon the Changing Breeds with the right Gift or Archid Form.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A thousand generations pass.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Migration:</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> For the purposes of calculating the effects of the Delirium treat humans as having +5 to their normal Willpower. Mokole caused Delirium is unaffected.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A thousand generations pass.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Flight and Extinction:</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Calculate the effect of Delirium as if humans have +3 to their normal Willpower. Mokole caused Delirium is unaffected.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A thousand generations pass.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Civilization:</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Calculate the effect of Delirium as if humans have +1 to their normal Willpower. Mokole caused Delirium is unaffected.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Two hundred generations pass.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Deluge:</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Calculate the effect of Delirium as if humans have +1 to their normal Willpower. Mokole caused Delirium is unaffected.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Fifty generations pass.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Poison:</b> Calculate the effect of Delirium as if humans have +1 to their normal Willpower. Mokole caused Delirium is unaffected.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Two hundred generations pass.<br /> <br /> <b>Reconciliation:</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">All backgrounds are now normal</span></span></span> <div align=\"center\">* * *</div> <br /> <br /> <br /> So for those interested, there ya go. I can't find where I wrote down my working for this scale, though I vaguely recall doing so. Looks to be every 500 generations of predation decreases the bonus to Willpower by one. Give or take.<br /> <br /> I had similar notes for Caerns, Human Invention, Gifts and Rites available, the Litany's development, Totems, Pure Breed, Ancestors, Fetishes and Talens, geographical ranges for Breeds, Species encompassed by Breeds, the rambling jottings of a timeline, Gauntlet strength, Moon Bridges, Tribe evolution... all sorts of stuff. Some cut for space, some cut for not meshing with other ideas. C'est la vie. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>And this is going in an appendix to the Timeline right off the bat, because this is actually hella cool. As far as your rambling jottings of a timeline...<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://cdn.meme.am/instances/500x/55515369.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> I would, in seriousness, be very interested to see it. And everything else, for that matter, but I'm a complete nutter completionist when it comes to the oWoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T18:20:16-08:00","id":1007511,"title":"","content":"Thank you <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"167\" data-vbnamecard=\"167\">nikink</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T18:44:41-08:00","id":1007517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nikink</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1005160-non-canon-exploration?p=1007155#post1007155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We're glad you like it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I've had a search and found some of my notes on the Delirium effect over the centuries. I reiterate the non-canonicity of this idea, and point out it wasn't developed beyond this first thought even though I kept it in mind to inform myself of the state of the world in each setting over time. <div align=\"center\">* * *</div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Delirium:</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The effects of the Delirium increase over time until they reach modern times. Prior to the Banestorm, Changing Breeds were no scarier in half-man form than animal form. Humans weren\u2019t being singled out and hunted. The humans had no concept of a separation between what was natural and what was supernatural. Post Banestorm as humans were fought over, and the various Kinfolk were hunted by shapeshifters waging war upon each other, the Delirium began. With each generation of humans the effects ever so slowly grew until modern times and modern effects. When the Impergium began the effect grew faster as humans became prey for Garou.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Banestorm:</b> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Delirium does not fully exist, treat all humans as having +7 effective Willpower - except for the Mokole who inflict it normally, including upon the Changing Breeds with the right Gift or Archid Form.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A thousand generations pass.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Migration:</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> For the purposes of calculating the effects of the Delirium treat humans as having +5 to their normal Willpower. Mokole caused Delirium is unaffected.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A thousand generations pass.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Flight and Extinction:</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Calculate the effect of Delirium as if humans have +3 to their normal Willpower. Mokole caused Delirium is unaffected.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A thousand generations pass.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Civilization:</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Calculate the effect of Delirium as if humans have +1 to their normal Willpower. Mokole caused Delirium is unaffected.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Two hundred generations pass.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Deluge:</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Calculate the effect of Delirium as if humans have +1 to their normal Willpower. Mokole caused Delirium is unaffected.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Fifty generations pass.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Poison:</b> Calculate the effect of Delirium as if humans have +1 to their normal Willpower. Mokole caused Delirium is unaffected.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Two hundred generations pass.<br /> <br /> <b>Reconciliation:</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">All backgrounds are now normal</span></span></span> <div align=\"center\">* * *</div> <br /> <br /> <br /> So for those interested, there ya go. I can't find where I wrote down my working for this scale, though I vaguely recall doing so. Looks to be every 500 generations of predation decreases the bonus to Willpower by one. Give or take.<br /> <br /> I had similar notes for Caerns, Human Invention, Gifts and Rites available, the Litany's development, Totems, Pure Breed, Ancestors, Fetishes and Talens, geographical ranges for Breeds, Species encompassed by Breeds, the rambling jottings of a timeline, Gauntlet strength, Moon Bridges, Tribe evolution... all sorts of stuff. Some cut for space, some cut for not meshing with other ideas. C'est la vie. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This right here is why I was so sad to see so few stretch goals reached. I was hoping to get the premade characters too (I wanted so bad to see what the writers would come up with when making a Ratkin Bard and an Ao....). I get not everyone was in it but losing everything listed here as possible stretch goal just burns so freaking much. If there was a way to still get this information as an expansion I'm being serious when I say i'm interested enough to pay for it.<br /> <br /> The way I see it, stretch goals go to the people who backed it as part of the KS payment...and I get that they were not earned. But I would gladly be a continued customer (and fanboy) to purchase this stuff, because I feel its a crying shame it doesn't get to see print. I remember a while back Rich Thomas (or was it Stew? someone important can't remember who now that I think on it) wasn't happy with the &quot;Take my money&quot; meme. And I don't mean to come off as that so much as a fan of shattered dreams, and the W20 line, and would LOVE to see the type of stuff Nik said he had made notes on (and the premade characters, I find the idea interesting because it gives me further incite from the authors).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","user":"CeltSPZ","date":". 11-23-2016, 10:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-24T03:46:59-08:00","id":1007639,"title":"","content":"So far as I'm aware, none of my notes would have, or even could have, ever been part of any Shattered Dreams stretch goals.<br /> Sample characters from all eras would have been cool, though. I'd love to delve into the Khara, Bards, and Ao. And the Eastern Breeds. Ah to dream. (No pun <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> #funfact: I remember catching myself a few times with names like 'Iron Fang' in periods long before iron was discovered. It was hella hard to try keeping all the Breeds' naming conventions consistent, across eras, and not anachronistic. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> My timeline really isn't special, by the way. It was almost literally as simple as going through wikipedia and jotting dates I thought important to remember down, organised into columns for different geographical regions. I supplemented that with everything I could glean from existing WoD books - bearing in mind very few referenced anything as far back as SD's eras. It was fun to re-read all those old books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-24T03:51:29-08:00","id":1007643,"title":"","content":"I've been doing a similar thing, which is why I'm so eager to see other timelines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-24T08:45:48-08:00","id":1007722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nikink</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1005160-non-canon-exploration?p=1007639#post1007639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So far as I'm aware, none of my notes would have, or even could have, ever been part of any Shattered Dreams stretch goals.<br /> Sample characters from all eras would have been cool, though. I'd love to delve into the Khara, Bards, and Ao. And the Eastern Breeds. Ah to dream. (No pun <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> #funfact: I remember catching myself a few times with names like 'Iron Fang' in periods long before iron was discovered. It was hella hard to try keeping all the Breeds' naming conventions consistent, across eras, and not anachronistic. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> My timeline really isn't special, by the way. It was almost literally as simple as going through wikipedia and jotting dates I thought important to remember down, organised into columns for different geographical regions. I supplemented that with everything I could glean from existing WoD books - bearing in mind very few referenced anything as far back as SD's eras. It was fun to re-read all those old books.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I mean....if they couldn't have even been stretch goals, would it be OK for you to share some of the stuff for those who are interested? I know it won't be canon, but it could still be a fun read for a lot of us who did enjoy your work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-24T20:52:01-08:00","id":1007928,"title":"","content":"Yep, sort of - NDA Ninjas are staking out my house (I can tell because I can't see them). I'm more than happy to share my thinking and my own house-rules. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Just remember it's all non-canonical 'fanon' around a non-canonical book - now the book is out, my ideas have no more weight than anyone else's.<br /> <br /> That said, I'm a bit pushed for time in the next couple of days, so I prolly won't post anything until Sunday/Monday at the earliest. Don't let that stop the discussion though! As a starter, why not create a characters for each setting as an exercise? Just a thought, I'd love to see what people come up with. Who plans on using the campaign as set up in the book? I know I'm excited to play through it. I figured getting excited to play in every setting meant we were on the right track - think how awful it'd be if we'd created a setting that bored us!<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}